t_and_push_tickets_branch acquires write_lock only around 'git add -A'/'commit' (push.py:392-440); the file is already on disk by then","push_after_commit docstring (push.py:452-461): txn/compact/delete 'do their own locked rename+commit' — i.e. the existing pattern writes INSIDE the lock, which this plan does not"],"finding":"The plan wires commit_and_push_tickets_branch at the _lib_ops caller AFTER set_project/remove_project return, so the projects.json read-modify-write (the actual state mutation) runs OUTSIDE the write lock — only the git add/commit runs under it. This under-delivers the very two-part invariant the plan enforces ('EVERY tickets-branch mutation runs under write_lock') and leaves a lost-update race between two concurrent set_project/remove_project calls, contradicting the plan's claim that they are 'durable + published under the write lock'.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f4b968040a3716bc6","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 2 / AC line 2 ('committed + pushed under the write lock')","norm_id":"nf3117265dcff6073","priority":0.9,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Two concurrent `rebar bridge projects set` invocations each read the mapping, mutate a different key, and write — the later write clobbers the earlier key (lost update) because neither RMW was serialized by the write lock","A reader observes a torn/stale mapping between the unlocked write and the locked commit"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.9,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_a